    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0155" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/8–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d95-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-18T15:00:00-04:00">August 18, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1861. Immediately upon information from Athens that Greek Govt concurs in
                    proposal for tripartite Allied supervision Greek elections please inform Soviet
                    FonOff developments along lines Deptel 1777 Aug. 9.<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d95-f2"/> Make clear that US Govt by signing Crimea communiqué
                    undertook responsibility to Greek people in contradistinction to present Greek
                    Govt in assisting them to express their will freely at the polls. Express US
                    Govt regret that Soviet Govt could not see its way clear to participate and
                    clearly state US Govts hope that Soviet Govt though not represented will adopt
                    friendly attitude toward this duty being undertaken by three of its Allies.
                    Assure Soviet FonOff that it will be kept fully informed of all developments in
                    Greece.</p>
                <p>Sent Moscow. Repeated to Athens, Paris, London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="91" type="source" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Athens, Paris, and London, as telegrams 828, 3886, and 7007,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d95-f2" n="92" xml:id="d95-f2-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 6704, August 9, 1 p.m., to London, <ref target="#pg134">p.
                        134</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
